{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"S1 ee8a re-review: BLOCK on G6 CRITICAL (impact 1.0) — validation ordering unspecified; if CR/LF/NUL checks run before ${env:VAR} substitution, an env var containing CRLF bypasses the injection guard (concrete scenario: value '${env:GATEWAY_TAG}' with GATEWAY_TAG='foo\\\\r\\\\nInjected: bar'). This is a real header-injection hole in the feature whose purpose is preventing it. Remediated: substitution runs first and every check applies to the fully resolved value, with a parametrized ordering regression test and an AC. Propagated the same rule to 26ae, whose ${run:...} substitution happens later at call time, so validation is re-applied on the substituted result there too."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787707035400559001,"uuid":"7ef98df4-71cf-4c9b-8c70-78c49fd6dbc1"}